---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Privacy & cookies';
const description = 'How Tangata Counselling handles personal information, cookies and third-party video content.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="article-hero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Privacy</div>
      <h1>{title}</h1>
    </div>
  </section>

  <article class="article-body">
    <p><strong>Last updated: 7 September 2026</strong></p>

    <p>I take privacy seriously, particularly because people contacting a counselling service may choose to share sensitive personal information.</p>
    <p>This notice explains how information is handled when you use the Tangata Counselling website or make an initial enquiry. If we agree to work together, I will also provide information about how client and counselling records are handled as part of our therapeutic agreement.</p>

    <h2>Who is responsible for your information?</h2>
    <p>Tangata Counselling is the private practice of <strong>Nick Tuftnell</strong>, a sole trader. I am the data controller for personal information processed through my private practice.</p>
    <p><strong>Address:</strong></p>
    <p>11 Everest Avenue<br />Fishponds<br />Bristol<br />BS16 2BY</p>
    <p><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:nick@tangata-counselling.co.uk">nick@tangata-counselling.co.uk</a></p>
    <p><strong>Telephone:</strong> <a href="tel:07988136267">07988 136267</a></p>
    <p>I am registered with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO).</p>

    <h2>When you visit this website</h2>
    <p>The website is hosted using <strong>Cloudflare</strong>. Like other web-hosting services, Cloudflare may process technical information needed to deliver and protect the website, such as your IP address, browser/device information, referring page and request information.</p>
    <p>My lawful basis for this processing is my <strong>legitimate interest</strong> in providing a secure, reliable and accessible website.</p>
    <p>Cloudflare is a global provider and some processing may take place outside the UK. Cloudflare publishes data-processing safeguards for international transfers.</p>
    <p>The website does not currently contain a contact form, booking system or payment system.</p>

    <h2>When you contact me</h2>
    <p>You can contact me by email or telephone. I may receive information such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>your name and contact details;</li>
      <li>the fact that you are interested in counselling or EMDR;</li>
      <li>information you choose to give me about what you are experiencing;</li>
      <li>correspondence about arranging an initial conversation or appointment.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Email is provided through <strong>Google Workspace</strong>.</p>
    <p>For counselling enquiries, my main lawful basis under UK GDPR is that processing is necessary to <strong>take steps at your request before entering into a contract</strong>, and subsequently to provide the counselling service if we agree to work together. BACP identifies this as an appropriate basis for counselling assessment and therapeutic contracting.</p>
    <p>Counselling enquiries can sometimes contain information about mental or physical health and other information classed as <strong>special-category data</strong>. I only use such information where it is relevant and necessary. Depending on the circumstances, an additional UK GDPR Article 9 condition may apply, including processing necessary for the establishment, exercise or defence of legal claims or for relevant safeguarding purposes. BACP notes that special-category information requires an Article 9 condition in addition to the ordinary Article 6 lawful basis.</p>
    <p>You do not need to send detailed information about your history or mental health in an initial email. A brief message asking to arrange a conversation is enough.</p>

    <h2>How long I keep enquiries</h2>
    <p>If you enquire but we do not go on to work together, I normally delete the enquiry and associated correspondence <strong>six weeks after our last meaningful contact</strong>.</p>
    <p>Where there is a genuine reason to expect that you may return shortly, I may retain it for up to <strong>three months</strong>.</p>
    <p>If you become a client, information relevant to our work may become part of the client record. My current routine retention period for adult client records is <strong>six years after the final counselling session</strong>, unless there is a specific reason to retain information longer, such as an ongoing safeguarding matter, complaint or legal process.</p>
    <p>BACP advises private practitioners to decide and agree a retention period with clients rather than retaining records indefinitely.</p>

    <h2>Who may receive your information?</h2>
    <p>I do not sell personal information or provide it to advertisers.</p>
    <p>Service providers currently involved in operating the website or handling initial enquiries include:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which hosts and protects the website;</li>
      <li><strong>Google Workspace</strong>, which provides my business email service.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These providers may use sub-processors or process information internationally subject to their contractual data-protection safeguards. Google Workspace provides data-processing terms for organisational customers.</p>
    <p>I may disclose information where I am legally required to do so or where disclosure is necessary in a serious safeguarding situation. More detailed confidentiality arrangements apply once counselling begins and are covered in the therapeutic agreement.</p>

    <h2>YouTube</h2>
    <p>Some pages contain YouTube videos.</p>
    <p>Tangata uses a <strong>privacy-preserving click-to-load player</strong>. When you first open the page, the video preview image is served by Tangata and your browser does <strong>not</strong> contact YouTube.</p>
    <p>Only when you deliberately choose <strong>Play video</strong> is the YouTube privacy-enhanced player loaded from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>.</p>
    <p>At that point YouTube becomes a separate third-party service and may process information or use browser storage according to its own privacy arrangements.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and analytics</h2>
    <p>At present:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Tangata does <strong>not</strong> use Google Analytics or another visitor analytics service;</li>
      <li>no advertising or remarketing pixels are installed;</li>
      <li>the website itself does not set cookies;</li>
      <li>it does not use localStorage, sessionStorage or similar persistent browser storage for tracking.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Because no non-essential tracking technology is currently running, Tangata does not currently display a general cookie-consent banner.</p>
    <p>If analytics, booking, payment or other technologies are introduced, I will review this notice <strong>before they go live</strong> and introduce consent controls where required.</p>
    <p>The ICO's current rules apply not only to traditional cookies but also to technologies such as tracking pixels, web storage, scripts and similar access technologies.</p>

    <h2>External links</h2>
    <p>The website links to other organisations and services, including professional bodies, research sources and social-media platforms.</p>
    <p>Those sites have their own privacy practices. Tangata does not send information to them merely because a link appears on the page; their services are contacted when you choose to follow the relevant link.</p>

    <h2>Your data-protection rights</h2>
    <p>Depending on the circumstances, you may have rights including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>access to personal information I hold about you;</li>
      <li>correction of inaccurate information;</li>
      <li>erasure of information where applicable;</li>
      <li>restriction of processing;</li>
      <li>objection to certain processing;</li>
      <li>data portability where applicable;</li>
      <li>withdrawal of consent where processing relies on consent.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>These rights are not absolute in every situation. For example, information may sometimes need to be retained for legal or safeguarding reasons.</p>
    <p>To exercise a right, contact me at <a href="mailto:nick@tangata-counselling.co.uk">nick@tangata-counselling.co.uk</a>.</p>
    <p>BACP notes that counselling clients have data-access rights and that records may sometimes be subject to lawful exceptions to disclosure.</p>

    <h2>Complaints</h2>
    <p>If you have concerns about how I handle your information, please contact me first and I will try to resolve them.</p>
    <p>You also have the right to complain to the <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a>, the UK's data-protection regulator.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this notice</h2>
    <p>I will review this notice when the website or the services I use materially change, and periodically as part of my data-protection review.</p>
    <p>Any significant new use of personal information will be reflected here before that processing begins.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>